\]

where \(I(x)\) is the invariant core, \(\mathcal{T}_I\) the transformations that preserve it, \(\mathcal{A}\) the actions it affords, and \(\Delta_{\text{interpretation}}\) the informative differences produced by different readers.

Meaning is therefore partly found, partly made, and most reliably recognized by what it continues to do across changed surfaces. The decoder is not digging up a motionless object; it is learning how to perform the relation.

